<article class="prose">
  <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
  <p><em>Last updated October 2026.</em></p>

  <p>By using {siteConfig.siteName}, you agree to these terms. They are written plainly on purpose: see
  <a href="/about/">about</a> for who runs this site and how.</p>

  <h2>What this site is</h2>
  <p>{siteConfig.siteName} is an automated local information site. Public information, such as council meeting
  papers, calendars and official alerts, is summarised by an AI language model and published without a person
  reviewing each item first. Items link back to their original source. See
  <a href="/how-we-gather-this/">how we gather this</a> and our
  <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> for the specifics.</p>

  <h2>Accuracy</h2>
  <p>We work to keep summaries accurate and grounded in their sources, and we correct mistakes when they are
  reported (see the <a href="/corrections/">corrections log</a>). But this is an automated site with no
  newsroom behind it: content is provided "as is", without a guarantee that it is complete, current or
  error-free. Always check the linked original source before relying on anything here for a decision that
  matters, such as a planning deadline, a closure or a meeting time. Nothing in these terms limits any right you
  have under consumer law that cannot be limited.</p>

  <h2>Using this site</h2>
  <p>You are welcome to read, link to and share pages from this site. Please do not scrape, republish or
  redistribute its content at scale without asking first; <a href="/contact/">get in touch</a> if you want to do
  something beyond normal reading and sharing.</p>
  <p>Content that comes from elsewhere (linked source documents, third-party sites) belongs to whoever made it.</p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>Summaries link to their original public source. We do not control those sites and are not responsible for
  their content or availability.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>These terms may be updated as the site changes. Continuing to use the site after a change means you accept
  the updated terms.</p>

  <p>Questions? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>.</p>
</article>

<style>
.prose { max-width: 40rem; }
